<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <%- include('partials/header') %>
    <style>
        .scoring-wrap {
            max-width: 880px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 1.5rem 1rem 4rem;
        }

        .scoring-hero {
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 2rem;
        }

        .scoring-hero .eyebrow {
            color: var(--primary-color);
        }

        .scoring-hero h1 {
            margin: 0.35rem 0 0.5rem;
        }

        .scoring-hero p {
            max-width: 46ch;
            margin: 0 auto;
            color: var(--text-muted);
        }

        .score-card {
            background: var(--bg-card);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
            box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
            padding: 1.5rem;
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
        }

        .score-card h2 {
            margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
        }

        .score-card .lead-sub {
            color: var(--text-muted);
            margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
        }

        /* ── Scoring table with an inline "value bar" so the doubling is visible ── */
        .scoring-table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
        }

        .scoring-table th,
        .scoring-table td {
            padding: 0.7rem 0.6rem;
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            text-align: left;
            vertical-align: middle;
        }

        .scoring-table thead th {
            font-size: 0.66rem;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.06em;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-weight: 700;
            white-space: nowrap;
        }

        .scoring-table tbody tr:last-child td {
            border-bottom: none;
        }

        .round-name {
            font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--text-main);
        }

        .round-sub {
            font-size: 0.72rem;
            color: var(--text-xmuted);
        }

        .pts {
            font-family: var(--mono);
            font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--text-main);
            white-space: nowrap;
        }

        .pts-big {
            font-size: 1.05rem;
            color: var(--primary-color);
        }

        .bar-cell {
            width: 38%;
            min-width: 120px;
        }

        .bar-track {
            background: var(--bg-softer);
            border-radius: 999px;
            height: 12px;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        .bar-fill {
            background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--primary-color), var(--primary-dark));
            height: 100%;
            border-radius: 999px;
        }

        .formula {
            font-family: var(--mono);
            background: var(--bg-soft);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            border-radius: var(--radius-md);
            padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
            color: var(--text-main);
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            display: inline-block;
        }

        .formula b {
            color: var(--primary-color);
        }

        .chain {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: 0.4rem;
            align-items: center;
            font-family: var(--mono);
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            margin-top: 0.75rem;
        }

        .chain .node {
            background: var(--primary-soft);
            color: var(--primary-dark);
            border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
            padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
            font-weight: 700;
        }

        .chain .op {
            color: var(--text-xmuted);
        }

        .why-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
            gap: 1rem;
            margin-top: 0.5rem;
        }

        .why-item {
            background: var(--bg-soft);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            border-radius: var(--radius-md);
            padding: 1rem;
        }

        .why-item h3 {
            margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
            font-size: 0.95rem;
        }

        .why-item p {
            margin: 0;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            line-height: 1.5;
        }

        .callout {
            border-left: 3px solid var(--primary-color);
            background: var(--primary-soft);
            border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
            padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
            color: var(--text-main);
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            line-height: 1.55;
        }

        /* ── Alternative-scheme comparison cards ── */
        .scheme {
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            border-radius: var(--radius-md);
            padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
            background: var(--bg-card);
        }

        .scheme.is-current {
            border-color: var(--primary-color);
            box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--primary-color);
            background: var(--primary-soft);
        }

        .scheme-head {
            display: flex;
            align-items: baseline;
            gap: 0.6rem;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
        }

        .scheme-head h3 {
            margin: 0;
            font-size: 1rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--text-main);
        }

        .scheme-badge {
            font-size: 0.62rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.05em;
            background: var(--primary-color);
            color: #fff;
            border-radius: 999px;
            padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem;
        }

        .scheme-seq {
            font-family: var(--mono);
            font-size: 0.8rem;
            color: var(--text-muted);
        }

        .scheme-body {
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            line-height: 1.5;
            margin: 0.5rem 0 0.9rem;
        }

        /* ── Top-5 mini bar chart inside each scheme card ── */
        .chart-label {
            font-size: 0.66rem;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.06em;
            color: var(--text-xmuted);
            font-weight: 700;
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        }

        .chart-row {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: 1.4rem minmax(0, 1fr) 2.6rem;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 0.5rem;
            margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
        }

        .chart-rank {
            font-family: var(--mono);
            font-size: 0.72rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--text-xmuted);
            text-align: right;
        }

        .chart-bar-wrap {
            position: relative;
            background: var(--bg-softer);
            border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
            height: 22px;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        .chart-bar {
            height: 100%;
            background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--primary-color), var(--primary-dark));
            border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
            min-width: 2px;
        }

        .is-current .chart-bar {
            background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--primary-color), var(--primary-dark));
        }

        .chart-name {
            position: absolute;
            left: 0.5rem;
            top: 50%;
            transform: translateY(-50%);
            font-size: 0.74rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            color: #fff;
            white-space: nowrap;
            text-shadow: 0 1px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
            pointer-events: none;
        }

        .chart-score {
            font-family: var(--mono);
            font-size: 0.78rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--text-main);
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <main class="scoring-wrap">
        <header class="scoring-hero">
            <div class="t-label eyebrow">How it works</div>
            <h1 class="t-display">The Scoring</h1>
            <p class="t-body">
                Pick <%= maxPicks %> teams &mdash; one from each seed line. You score points every time one of
                your teams wins a game. The deeper a team runs, the more each win is worth.
            </p>
        </header>

        <!-- ── The point schedule ── -->
        <section class="score-card">
            <h2 class="t-h2">Points per win, by round</h2>
            <p class="lead-sub t-small">
                Seed doesn&rsquo;t matter for scoring &mdash; a 10-seed&rsquo;s win in the Sweet 16 is worth exactly
                the same as a 1-seed&rsquo;s.
            </p>

            <%
              // Scale every bar against the biggest round value so the doubling
              // is visually obvious without a charting library.
              const maxRoundPoints = rows.reduce((m, r) => Math.max(m, r.roundPoints), 0);
            %>
            <table class="scoring-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Round</th>
                        <th>Win is worth</th>
                        <th class="bar-cell">Relative value</th>
                        <th>Team total*</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <% rows.forEach(function (r) { %>
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <div class="round-name"><%= r.name %></div>
                            <div class="round-sub">Round <%= r.round %></div>
                        </td>
                        <td><span class="pts pts-big">+<%= r.roundPoints %></span></td>
                        <td class="bar-cell">
                            <div class="bar-track">
                                <div class="bar-fill"
                                    style="width: <%= Math.round((r.roundPoints / maxRoundPoints) * 100) %>%;"></div>
                            </div>
                        </td>
                        <td><span class="pts"><%= r.cumulative %></span></td>
                    </tr>
                    <% }); %>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="round-sub" style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
                *Team total = points a single team has earned for you by reaching that round (each win added up).
                The First Four play-in games award <strong>0 points</strong>.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- ── Why these numbers ── -->
        <section class="score-card">
            <h2 class="t-h2">Why these numbers?</h2>
            <p class="lead-sub t-small">The schedule isn&rsquo;t arbitrary &mdash; it follows one simple rule.</p>

            <p class="t-body" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                Each round is worth <strong>(2&times; the previous round) &minus; 1</strong>. Winning a game is
                always worth a little less than everything that team earned to get there &mdash; so advancing keeps
                getting more valuable, but earlier rounds never become meaningless.
            </p>

            <div class="formula">
                roundPoints(n) = 2 &times; roundPoints(n&minus;1) &minus; 1 = <b>2<sup>n&minus;1</sup> + 1</b>
            </div>

            <div class="chain">
                <% rows.forEach(function (r, i) { %>
                    <% if (i > 0) { %><span class="op">&rarr;</span><% } %>
                    <span class="node">+<%= r.roundPoints %></span>
                <% }); %>
            </div>
            <p class="round-sub" style="margin-top: 0.6rem;">
                2&rarr;3&rarr;5&rarr;9&rarr;17&rarr;33 &mdash; each value is double the last, minus one.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- ── What it means for strategy ── -->
        <section class="score-card">
            <h2 class="t-h2">What it means for your picks</h2>
            <div class="why-grid">
                <div class="why-item">
                    <h3>Depth beats breadth</h3>
                    <p>
                        One team reaching the Final Four (36 pts) outscores three teams that each win a single
                        opening-round game (6 pts). Find teams that can <em>run</em>.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="why-item">
                    <h3>Underdogs pay the same</h3>
                    <p>
                        Because seed never affects points, a Cinderella low seed that goes deep is pure upside &mdash;
                        identical reward, lower ownership against the field.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="why-item">
                    <h3>Early wins still matter</h3>
                    <p>
                        The &minus;1 keeps the curve from running away. A wall of first-round wins keeps you in it
                        while you wait for a deep run to break the tie.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="why-item">
                    <h3>The ceiling is everything</h3>
                    <p>
                        With each round nearly doubling, your <em>possible</em> points hinge almost entirely on how
                        far your best team can go &mdash; that&rsquo;s what the rankings project.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="callout" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
                Bottom line: the most points wins. Spread your seeds, but spend your real bets on teams you believe
                can survive the second weekend &mdash; that&rsquo;s where the points live.
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- ── Other ways to score ── -->
        <section class="score-card">
            <h2 class="t-h2">Other ways we could score it</h2>
            <p class="lead-sub t-small">
                The point schedule is a choice, and it completely changes who wins. Our scheme is shown first as a
                reference, followed by the other common options &mdash; each with how the
                <strong>top 5 of the 2026 field</strong> would actually have finished under it. Same brackets, same
                results, different math.
            </p>

            <% schemes.forEach(function (s) { %>
            <div class="scheme<%= s.current ? ' is-current' : '' %>">
                <div class="scheme-head">
                    <h3><%= s.name %></h3>
                    <% if (s.current) { %><span class="scheme-badge">What we use</span><% } %>
                    <span class="scheme-seq"><%= s.points.join(' · ') %></span>
                </div>
                <p class="round-sub" style="margin:0;"><%= s.tagline %></p>
                <p class="scheme-body"><%= s.body %></p>

                <div class="chart-label">Top 5 of the 2026 field under this scheme</div>
                <% s.chart.entries.forEach(function (e) { %>
                <div class="chart-row">
                    <div class="chart-rank">#<%= e.rank %></div>
                    <div class="chart-bar-wrap">
                        <div class="chart-bar"
                            style="width: <%= Math.max(2, Math.round((e.score / s.chart.max) * 100)) %>%;"></div>
                        <span class="chart-name"><%= e.name %></span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="chart-score"><%= e.score %></div>
                </div>
                <% }); %>
            </div>
            <% }); %>

            <div class="callout" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
                Look at how the order moves. <strong>Nothing but Net</strong> finishes 4th under our scheme but would
                crater to <strong>34th</strong> if every win counted the same &mdash; it had few wins but deep ones.
                <strong>Go Terps</strong> does the opposite: 2nd on pure win-count, only 5th under ours. Flat scoring
                rewards lucky breadth; pure doubling turns the whole pool into one bet on the champion. The
                double-minus-one curve is the compromise that rewards the skill of picking a team that <em>runs</em>,
                without throwing away everyone whose champion bows out early.
            </div>
        </section>

        <div class="text-center">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/">Back to Bracket 10</a>
        </div>
    </main>

    <%- include('partials/scripts') %>
</body>

</html>
